NOTES_HTML='''<p>Michelin: the 2026 California selection, announced June 24, 2026 in San Diego. Los Angeles holds twenty-five stars — Somni and Providence at three (the city's first, awarded in 2025); Kato promoted to two beside n/naka, Hayato and Mélisse; five new one-stars in Corridor 109, Kojima, Lielle, Miura and Seline — while 715, Camphor and Morihiro (after its move to Echo Park) lost theirs. Forty-one Bib Gourmands, with Little Fish and Sonoratown added; Little Fish's chefs were named Michelin's Young Chefs of the Year. Providence holds a Green Star.</p><p>Bars: Thunderbolt in Echo Park is LA's North America's 50 Best regular and a James Beard Outstanding Bar finalist. The Varnish's rebirth behind Cole's and Clifton's reopening are flagged to verify.</p><p>Occasion chips for Los Angeles are editorial assignments, by category and price. Tock runs the omakase counters and the three-stars; Resy the rest; the scene restaurants of West Hollywood book on SevenRooms. The Amex credit works at Resy and Tock.</p><p>Photography via Pexels (royalty-free): three photographs, cropped and reused across the twelve sections.</p>'''
